        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Shawl of woven silk and wool. The main colours are red, green and yellow. It also contains white, blue and brown. The shawl is covered with a pattern consisting of a complex medallion extending lengthwise to meet the upper lobes of a cartouche central at each end, and containing a flowering plant form. To either side of these central features curve the elongated cone forms with feathery ends.\n\nAt either end the warp has been given the colours of the small panels of decoration in red, yellow, white, green, blue and brown. These coloured warp ends form the fringe, unknotted except for the last 4.5 inches, held in place by 0.125 inch red weft woven across the warp threads in groups of three. The weave is a compound tabby, very finely woven, and the weft is all of wool on a warp of wool twisted with silk."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/af1c2848-18a2-3ed4-b910-516203fdc918> .

